A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is not reflexive. For example, $3∣3.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is not symmetric. For example, $9∤3$ but $3∣9.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is not transitive. For example, $3∤2$ and $2∤9,$ but $3∣9.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is not an equivalence relation since it's neither reflexive nor symmetric nor transitive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421413 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152068 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7f9502e-19c3-58bb-98da-1562e0b0dfd0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4af48504-6f1c-5b90-87ab-46f546fb2eb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421329} {:answer/id #uuid "6d984c53-eae2-5d52-bffe-bead8d751ef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421346} {:answer/id #uuid "810ae78b-09ba-5372-b677-ed900baea3aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421351} {:answer/id #uuid "8a83063d-29fe-5569-893d-885aaf2bcb4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421353} {:answer/id #uuid "d179e1fc-abb6-5aca-92d5-246063f7fbc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4af48504-6f1c-5b90-87ab-46f546fb2eb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421329}